      en: "The facility in New Halfa was built to provide employment for displaced people from the Wadi Halfa area and to strengthen the region's economy. Part of a resettlement project. Benefits from the Khashm el-Girba Dam. Sugar for the east of the country. Important economic factor in Kassala. Thus, the site is among the characteristic points of Sudan along the Nile, the Nubian Desert and the Red Sea, and offers insight into the ancient Nubian heritage and the regional identity."
